<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Sell on Shopping Paradise', cartCount, seller }) %>

<div class="pricing-page">
  <h1>Sell on Shopping Paradise For Deals</h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">One simple plan. No listing fees, no surprises.</p>

  <div class="price-card">
    <h2>Seller plan</h2>
    <p class="price big">$14<span class="muted">/month</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>4% per sale</strong> marketplace fee — taken from the sale, never added to the buyer's price</li>
      <li>Unlimited product listings</li>
      <li><strong>Transparent shipping:</strong> your item price is shown as-is; you set shipping rates separately and they're added at checkout for every destination — nothing hidden</li>
      <li>Seller dashboard with orders and fee reporting</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/seller/signup">Start selling</a> <span class="muted small">(demo — no real billing)</span></p>
  </div>

  <h2>How the 4% works</h2>
  <p>You list a hoodie at $74.99. The buyer sees <strong>$74.99</strong> plus the shipping you set — for example, $7.99 Standard — and tax, all shown as separate lines at checkout. When it sells, the 4% marketplace fee comes out of your proceeds on the goods-plus-shipping amount — the buyer never pays a cent more than the shown lines.</p>

  <h2>How shipping works</h2>
  <p>Enter your item price and four shipping rates when you list a product: Standard and Express for Canada &amp; the USA, and Standard and Express for other countries. (Leave an Express rate blank to offer Express at the Standard rate — we never multiply or estimate.) Buyers choose Standard or Express at checkout; the shipping they pay goes to you. Every order ships via your country's national postal service.</p>
</div>

